displays the returned password-reset confirmation or error message\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall provide System Administrator screens to create and deactivate accounts and assign roles, staff warehouse access, and customer-organisation access.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-2\",\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A System Administrator is viewing account management\",\n     \"when\": \"the administrator opens an account or submits account or access changes\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays account fields and the returned status or error message\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.2\",\n     \"given\": \"A user without the System Administrator role opens account management\",\n     \"when\": \"the page loads\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays an access-denied message or the account-management page is not displayed\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n   \"ears\": \"When a driver opens today's routes, the Meridian web app shall show only that driver's assigned routes and each route's stops in route order.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"ASM-5\",\n    \"ASM-8\",\n    \"Q-2\",\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"I-2\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.1\",\n     \"given\": \"Route data contains routes assigned to multiple drivers\",\n     \"when\": \"a driver opens today's route list\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen lists only routes returned or assigned to that driver and displays each route's stops in order\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall compare scanned shipper boxes with expected boxes before route departure, report missing or wrong-route boxes, and keep departure blocked until all expected boxes are scanned and wrong boxes are removed or corrected.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"ASM-8\",\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-10\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A route has an expected box that has not been scanned\",\n     \"when\": \"the driver attempts to complete loading or depart\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the missing-box status and keeps the departure control unavailable\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.2\",\n     \"given\": \"The driver scans a box assigned to another route\",\n     \"when\": \"the scan is processed\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows a wrong-route warning naming the box and keeps departure blocked\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.3\",\n     \"given\": \"Every expected box is scanned and no wrong-route box remains\",\n     \"when\": \"the driver completes loading\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows loading complete and displays an enabled departure control\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-5\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall show dispatchers each route stop's status and last-updated time.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"ASM-5\",\n    \"ASM-9\",\n    \"I-9\",\n    \"I-10\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.1\",\n     \"given\": \"The route service returns stop statuses and update-time fields\",\n     \"when\": \"a dispatcher opens route monitoring\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays each stop's returned status and last-updated time\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-6\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall show each route box's latest available temperature, status, and alerts from the supplied gateway data and identify cached temperature data as stale while disconnected.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"ASM-12\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"I-21\",\n    \"I-42\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.1\",\n     \"given\": \"The gateway feed returns temperature, status, and alert data for route boxes\",\n     \"when\": \"the driver opens route monitoring\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays each box's current temperature, status, and returned alerts\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.2\",\n     \"given\": \"The browser is disconnected and cached temperature data is available\",\n     \"when\": \"the driver opens box monitoring\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays the cached temperature value and marks it stale\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-7\",\n   \"ears\": \"When scanned stock is On Hold, the Meridian web app shall display “Do not deliver” and the returned hold reason and prevent handover of that box.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"ASM-1\",\n    \"ASM-10\",\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"I-11\",\n    \"I-14\",\n    \"I-16\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A stop includes a scanned box whose returned stock status is On Hold\",\n     \"when\": \"the driver opens that box's handover controls\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays “Do not deliver” and the hold reason and offers no enabled handover control for that box\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.2\",\n     \"given\": \"A stop includes both On Hold and deliverable boxes\",\n     \"when\": \"the driver opens the handover screen\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen permits handover only for deliverable boxes\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-8\",\n   \"ears\": \"When online, if a scanned box is reported as Recalled, the Meridian web app shall display “Do not deliver” and prevent handover of that box.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-3\",\n    \"ASM-10\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A driver is online and the service reports a scanned box as Recalled\",\n     \"when\": \"the driver opens that box's handover controls\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays “Do not deliver” and no enabled handover control for that box\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-9\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall let drivers record an eligible handover with receiver name, signature, delivery photo, actual handover time, and available browser location.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"ASM-11\",\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"I-12\",\n    \"Q-4\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A box is eligible for handover\",\n     \"when\": \"the driver enters the receiver name, captures a signature and photo, and completes handover\",\n     \"then\": \"the handover request contains the receiver, signature, photo, actual completion time, and available location fields\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n   \"ears\": \"If browser location is denied or unavailable, then the Meridian web app shall allow an otherwise eligible handover and record location as unavailable.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"ASM-11\",\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"I-12\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.1\",\n     \"given\": \"Browser location access is denied or unavailable\",\n     \"when\": \"the driver completes an otherwise eligible handover\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays the completed handover and a location-unavailable value, and the request records location as unavailable\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-11\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall let drivers record full or partial refusal only by whole box and require a reason for each refused box.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-7\",\n    \"I-6\",\n    \"I-7\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A driver is recording a refusal\",\n     \"when\": \"the driver selects refused boxes and submits a reason for each\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays each refused whole box with its reason and offers no partial-box quantity control\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.2\",\n     \"given\": \"The service returns a refusal and quarantine result\",\n     \"when\": \"the driver opens the completed refusal\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned refusal status and quarantine status for each refused box\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-12\",\n   \"ears\": \"While offline, the Meridian web app shall retain loading, handover, and refusal work locally across session expiry or sign-out, automatically send queued work when connectivity returns after re-authentication if needed, preserve the handover's occurrence time, and reuse the same handover identifier on retries.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"ASM-5\",\n    \"ASM-11\",\n    \"I-7\",\n    \"I-8\",\n    \"I-9\",\n    \"I-14\",\n    \"I-16\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.1\",\n     \"given\": \"The browser is offline\",\n     \"when\": \"the driver records loading, handover, or refusal work\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows each action in the pending queue and retains its entered values\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.2\",\n     \"given\": \"Queued work exists and connectivity returns\",\n     \"when\": \"the web app reconnects\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows queued work being sent without requiring resubmission, and displays the returned sync status\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.3\",\n     \"given\": \"A handover was recorded offline\",\n     \"when\": \"the web app sends it or retries an interrupted send\",\n     \"then\": \"the request contains the original handover time and the same handover identifier as the original request\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.4\",\n     \"given\": \"Loading, handover, or refusal work, including handover signature and photo values, is queued while offline and the driver session expires or the driver signs out\",\n     \"when\": \"the driver re-authenticates and the connection returns\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen lists the retained queued work and its entered values, and the request sends the work without requiring re-entry\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-13\",\n   \"ears\": \"When an assigned route changes while a driver is offline, the Meridian web app shall show route differences, require review and resolution of affected unsent work before continuing, and preserve completed offline handovers.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"ASM-9\",\n    \"I-8\",\n    \"I-14\",\n    \"I-16\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.1\",\n     \"given\": \"The route returned after reconnection differs and unsent work exists\",\n     \"when\": \"the driver reconnects and the app reconciles the route\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen lists route differences and affected boxes requiring review\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.2\",\n     \"given\": \"Route differences have unresolved affected boxes\",\n     \"when\": \"the driver attempts to continue route work\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen blocks continuing and shows the unresolved boxes\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.3\",\n     \"given\": \"A handover was completed offline before the route changed\",\n     \"when\": \"the new route is synchronized\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen still displays the completed handover and its original time\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-14\",\n   \"ears\": \"When an offline handover conflicts with a hold or recall upon synchronization, the Meridian web app shall retain and flag the handover and display the returned quality-case result.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"ASM-10\",\n    \"I-14\",\n    \"I-16\",\n    \"I-41\",\n    \"I-46\",\n    \"I-47\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.1\",\n     \"given\": \"An offline handover is synchronized and the service returns a hold or recall conflict and quality-case result\",\n     \"when\": \"the driver or quality user opens the synchronized record\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays the retained handover, conflict flag, and returned quality-case status\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-15\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall show Quality reviewers the full excursion temperature history, allowance used and remaining for each tier, and the returned recommendation, using the configured tier rules.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-8\",\n    \"ASM-12\",\n    \"I-21\",\n    \"I-22\",\n    \"I-23\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.1\",\n     \"given\": \"An excursion review receives temperature history, tier budgets, and a recommendation\",\n     \"when\": \"a Quality reviewer opens the affected handling unit\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays the full history, used and remaining allowance for each tier, and the recommendation\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.2\",\n     \"given\": \"Configured tier limits and allowances are returned for different products\",\n     \"when\": \"a user views settings or excursion reviews for those products\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays the same configured tier-limit and allowance values for each product\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-16\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall present a single-person quality-decision flow only for an excursion within the first tier above or below the permitted band with allowance remaining, and otherwise present a Quality Officer proposal and separate approval by a different Quality Manager; written justification is required when a decision opposes the recommendation.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"ASM-13\",\n    \"I-24\",\n    \"I-25\",\n    \"I-26\",\n    \"I-27\",\n    \"I-28\",\n    \"I-29\",\n    \"I-30\",\n    \"I-31\",\n    \"I-32\",\n    \"I-33\",\n    \"Q-6\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-16.1\",\n     \"given\": \"An excursion is within the first tier above or below the band and has allowance remaining\",\n     \"when\": \"an eligible Quality Officer opens the decision form\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays the single-person decision controls\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-16.2\",\n     \"given\": \"An excursion is outside the single-person case or has no allowance remaining\",\n     \"when\": \"a Quality Officer opens the decision form\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen requires a proposal and separate Quality Manager approval\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-16.3\",\n     \"given\": \"The proposing Quality Officer also has the Quality Manager role\",\n     \"when\": \"that person attempts to approve the proposal\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen does not offer an approval action to that same person\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-16.4\",\n     \"given\": \"A proposed decision opposes the displayed recommendation\",\n     \"when\": \"a user prepares the decision\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen requires both decision participants and a written-justification field\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-17\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall require identity confirmation using the account's sign-in method and a reason when a user signs a quality decision, and present signed decisions as read-only with a separate superseding-decision action.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"ASM-1\",\n    \"ASM-13\",\n    \"I-25\",\n    \"I-33\",\n    \"I-34\",\n    \"I-35\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-17.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A user is ready to sign a quality decision\",\n     \"when\": \"the user submits the signing form\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen requires identity confirmation and a reason before showing the signed-decision status\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-17.2\",\n     \"given\": \"A decision is returned as signed\",\n     \"when\": \"a user opens that decision\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows signed values as read-only, provides a separate superseding-decision action, and offers no edit or delete control\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-17.3\",\n     \"given\": \"The service returns an earlier signed decision and a superseding decision\",\n     \"when\": \"a reviewer opens decision history\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays both signed decision records and identifies the superseding decision\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-18\",\n   \"ears\": \"When the service returns a quality disposition, the Meridian web app shall show resulting stock, order, and route status and the earlier and current disposition when superseded.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"ASM-1\",\n    \"I-34\",\n    \"I-35\",\n    \"I-36\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-18.1\",\n     \"given\": \"The service returns a release, rejection, or superseding disposition\",\n     \"when\": \"a Quality user views the affected stock or handling unit\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned stock, order, and route status and disposition history\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-18.2\",\n     \"given\": \"The service rejects a superseding disposition because its reversal cannot be applied after stock was delivered or destroyed\",\n     \"when\": \"a Quality user views the affected stock or handling unit\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned error and unchanged returned stock, order, and route status, and does not present the superseding disposition as applied\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-19\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall collect destruction date, quantity, and witness for rejected stock and prevent entry of quantity greater than the displayed rejected quantity.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-36\",\n    \"I-37\",\n    \"I-38\",\n    \"ASM-1\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-19.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A user opens destruction entry for rejected stock\",\n     \"when\": \"the user records destruction\",\n     \"then\": \"the request contains destruction date, quantity, and witness fields\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-19.2\",\n     \"given\": \"The entered destruction quantity exceeds the displayed rejected quantity\",\n     \"when\": \"the user submits the entry\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows a validation error and sends no destruction request\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-20\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall identify quality decisions waiting more than four hours as escalated in the Quality Manager's waiting-decisions view.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-37\",\n    \"I-38\",\n    \"ASM-3\",\n    \"ASM-14\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-20.1\",\n     \"given\": \"The service returns a decision waiting more than four hours as escalated\",\n     \"when\": \"a Quality Manager opens waiting decisions\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen lists the decision and displays its escalated status\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.3333333333333333\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-21\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall provide a Quality Manager flow to start and close recalls with signed actions, collecting product, one or more lots, reason, and severity for recall start, and display each returned action result.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-3\",\n    \"Q-6\",\n    \"I-39\",\n    \"I-40\",\n    \"I-41\",\n    \"ASM-4\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-21.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A Quality Manager opens recall start\",\n     \"when\": \"the manager enters product, lot numbers, reason, severity, and signature\",\n     \"then\": \"the recall request contains those values and the screen displays the returned recall result\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-21.2\",\n     \"given\": \"A Quality Manager closes a recall\",\n     \"when\": \"the manager submits the signed close action\",\n     \"then\": \"the close request contains the signature and the screen displays the returned close status or error message\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-21.3\",\n     \"given\": \"A user who is not identified as eligible to manage recalls opens recall management\",\n     \"when\": \"recall actions load\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen does not display recall start or close actions\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-22\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall display the returned recall trace, including warehouse locations, boxes, routes, customer deliveries, quantities, delivery dates, receivers, and the trace total alongside received quantity when supplied.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-3\",\n    \"ASM-7\",\n    \"ASM-12\",\n    \"I-41\",\n    \"I-42\",\n    \"I-43\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-22.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A recall trace response contains affected locations and delivery records\",\n     \"when\": \"a Quality Manager opens the trace\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays each returned warehouse, box, route, customer delivery, quantity, delivery date, and receiver\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-22.2\",\n     \"given\": \"The service returns trace quantities and the lot's total received quantity\",\n     \"when\": \"the user views the trace summary\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned trace total alongside the received quantity\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-23\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall show customer recall notices in the portal, link notices to affected deliveries, and provide a response entry point.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"ASM-4\",\n    \"ASM-15\",\n    \"I-41\",\n    \"I-44\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-23.1\",\n     \"given\": \"The service returns an active recall notice for the signed-in customer's organisation\",\n     \"when\": \"the customer opens the portal\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays the recall notice, its returned status, affected deliveries, and a response entry point\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-24\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall let customers submit per-delivery on-hand, used or dispensed, and destroyed quantities, allow a total below the delivered amount as unaccounted, and reject a total above it.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-3\",\n    \"I-41\",\n    \"I-45\",\n    \"I-46\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-24.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A customer opens a recall response for a delivery\",\n     \"when\": \"the customer enters on-hand, used or dispensed, and destroyed quantities\",\n     \"then\": \"the response request contains the entered quantity fields for that delivery\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-24.2\",\n     \"given\": \"The reported quantities total less than the delivered quantity\",\n     \"when\": \"the customer submits the response\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen accepts the values and displays the difference as unaccounted quantity\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-24.3\",\n     \"given\": \"The reported quantities exceed the delivered quantity\",\n     \"when\": \"the customer submits the response\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays a validation error or returned error message and sends no invalid response request\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-25\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall show recall progress as the returned percentage accounted for, identify outstanding customers and reminder status when supplied, and let a Quality Manager submit a signed write-off justification for unaccounted quantity.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-3\",\n    \"Q-6\",\n    \"ASM-15\",\n    \"I-41\",\n    \"I-46\",\n    \"I-47\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-25.1\",\n     \"given\": \"The service returns recall progress and outstanding customers\",\n     \"when\": \"a Quality Manager opens recall progress\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays the accounted percentage and outstanding-customer list\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-25.2\",\n     \"given\": \"The service returns customer response and reminder statuses\",\n     \"when\": \"a user opens recall progress\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned reminder status\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-25.3\",\n     \"given\": \"A Quality Manager selects unaccounted quantity for write-off\",\n     \"when\": \"the manager submits the write-off\",\n     \"then\": \"the request contains a signed justification and the screen displays the returned write-off status or refusal message\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-25.4\",\n     \"given\": \"A recall has unaccounted quantity without a signed write-off\",\n     \"when\": \"a Quality Manager attempts to close the recall\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen blocks submission and displays the outstanding quantity or returned close error\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-26\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall show customers only their organisation's current and past orders, allocated lots and expiry dates, order status, and in-transit delivery arrival and temperature status, without exposing other route customers.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-2\",\n    \"ASM-16\",\n    \"ASM-17\",\n    \"I-48\",\n    \"I-49\",\n    \"I-50\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-26.1\",\n     \"given\": \"The service returns orders and delivery data for a customer's organisation and other organisations\",\n     \"when\": \"the customer opens the orders page\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen lists only that organisation's orders and displays returned status, lots, and expiry dates\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-26.2\",\n     \"given\": \"The service returns an in-transit delivery with arrival and temperature status\",\n     \"when\": \"the customer views the delivery\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays planned arrival and in-range or out-of-range status and no other customer's identity or delivery details\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-27\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall provide a PDF certificate for each completed delivery with products, lots, expiry dates, quantities, receiver, handover time, each box's temperature chart from sealing to handover, excursions, and signed excursion decisions.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-4\",\n    \"ASM-16\",\n    \"ASM-18\",\n    \"I-50\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-27.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A completed delivery has a certificate available\",\n     \"when\": \"the customer selects certificate download\",\n     \"then\": \"the downloaded file is a PDF containing the listed delivery, handover, temperature, excursion, and decision fields\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-28\",\n   \"ears\": \"When late readings produce a new certificate version, the Meridian web app shall list the new and earlier versions and keep each available for download.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-4\",\n    \"ASM-18\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-28.1\",\n     \"given\": \"The service returns a new certificate version and retains the earlier version\",\n     \"when\": \"the customer opens certificate history\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen lists both versions and provides a file download link for each\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-29\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall present the customer portal and certificates in the user's selected English or Arabic, render Arabic right to left including tables and charts, and show dates and times in the account's configured time zone.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"ASM-6\",\n    \"ASM-16\",\n    \"ASM-18\",\n    \"I-13\",\n    \"I-15\",\n    \"I-17\",\n    \"I-18\",\n    \"I-19\",\n    \"I-20\",\n    \"I-50\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-29.1\",\n     \"given\": \"The user selects Arabic\",\n     \"when\": \"the portal and a delivery certificate are displayed\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen and certificate display Arabic content with right-to-left direction for tables and charts\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-29.2\",\n     \"given\": \"The user's account has a configured time zone\",\n     \"when\": \"the portal displays order or delivery dates and times\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays the values in that configured time zone\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-30\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall provide an audit-trail screen showing returned entries with actor, time, changed fields, old and new values, and supplied reason, with filters by record, user, date range, and action type and export of the filtered view.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-4\",\n    \"I-13\",\n    \"I-15\",\n    \"I-17\",\n    \"I-18\",\n    \"I-19\",\n    \"I-20\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-30.1\",\n     \"given\": \"Audit entries are returned for multiple records, users, dates, and action types\",\n     \"when\": \"an Auditor opens the audit trail\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays each entry's actor, time, changed fields, old and new values, and supplied reason\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-30.2\",\n     \"given\": \"An Auditor selects audit filters\",\n     \"when\": \"the filters are applied and the Auditor exports the view\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays the matching returned list and provides a file containing the filtered view\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-31\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall show the returned history of a lot from receipt through delivery or destruction in time order.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-4\",\n    \"Q-5\",\n    \"ASM-1\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-31.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A lot-history response contains receipt, movement, delivery, or destruction events\",\n     \"when\": \"an Auditor opens lot history\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned events in time order\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-32\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall provide on-screen reports for selected date ranges and warehouses, with CSV export of displayed report figures, including the specified excursion, refusal/destruction, delivery, decision-time, expiry, and recall measures.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"ASM-2\",\n    \"ASM-15\",\n    \"I-50\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-32.1\",\n     \"given\": \"The service returns report figures for selected date range and warehouse\",\n     \"when\": \"staff open the reports screen\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays every specified report measure and its returned value\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-32.2\",\n     \"given\": \"A staff user has warehouse access scope\",\n     \"when\": \"the user filters reports and exports them\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen offers only in-scope warehouses and the downloaded CSV file contains the displayed filtered figures\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-33\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall provide forms to enter opening lots and stock records and submit them to the service.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-20\",\n    \"Q-5\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-33.1\",\n     \"given\": \"An authorized staff user opens opening-inventory entry\",\n     \"when\": \"the user enters lot and stock details\",\n     \"then\": \"the request contains the entered opening lot and stock fields and the screen displays the returned result or error\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-34\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall make recorded handover signatures and delivery photos available from a delivery record within its seven-year evidence-retention period.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-4\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-34.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A delivery record within its retention period includes signature and photo evidence\",\n     \"when\": \"an authorized user opens the delivery record\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays the signature and photo fields or their available file links\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n   \"metric\": \"All pages render without horizontal scrolling at widths from 320 px through 1920 px; interactive touch targets on narrow viewports are at least 44 by 44 CSS px.\",\n   \"text\": \"The Meridian web app shall be responsive on phone, tablet, and desktop browsers, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n   \"text\": \"The Meridian web app shall support the latest two browser versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.\",\n   \"metric\": \"100% of primary driver and customer flow acceptance tests pass on the latest 2 released versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n   \"metric\": \"Automated accessibility checks report zero applicable WCAG 2.1 AA violations on main flows and manual keyboard checks pass.\",\n   \"text\": \"The main web-app flows shall conform to WCAG 2.1 AA.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-4\",\n   \"metric\": \"For responses containing up to 100,000 records, all returned trace entries are displayed or accessible within 60 seconds after the response is received.\",\n   \"text\": \"The web app shall render the full recall trace returned by the service for the assumed launch scale.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-5\",\n   \"metric\": \"With fixtures representing 1,000 users and 100,000 records, the trace screen displays the complete returned trace within 60 seconds of the user's request.\",\n   \"text\": \"The web client shall support the assumed first-year product scale and make a requested lot trace available through its screen within the requested time limit.\"\n  }\n ],\n \"outOfScope\": [\n  \"API-side enforcement of credentials, password-reset token validity/delivery, role and access-scope authorization, and account state; web requirements cover forms, requests, screens, and API response handling.\",\n  \"API-side persistence and enforcement of stock/order/route transitions, hold and recall blocking across warehouses, quarantine, quantity validation/conservation, recall trace completeness and arithmetic, recall closure eligibility, write-off authorization, and duplicate-handover idempotency.\",\n  \"API-side audit creation, tamper detection, immutability, seven-year retention of audit records and handover evidence, and certificate-version persistence.\",\n  \"API-side scheduled and outbound emails, including recall notices and 24-hour reminders, four-hour decision escalation, daily summaries, monthly reports, and monthly report generation; web screens display supplied results/status where specified.\",\n  \"API-side production of recall traces within a time limit; the client timing requirements measure rendering after the response or from the user's request, as specified in separate requirements.\",\n  \"Supplying live temperature readings, alerts, box associations, and history through the existing logger or supplier gateway feed.\",\n  \"Importing or guaranteeing initial database contents; the web app provides opening-lot and stock entry.\",\n  \"Pricing, invoicing and payments; route stop-order optimization; manufacturer purchasing and demand forecasting; automatic driver or customer penalties; stock transfers between warehouses; logger hardware and supplier gateway implementation.\",\n  \"Native iOS or Android applications, app-store distribution, push notifications, and background location. The product is a responsive web app; applicable notices use in-app notices or email, location uses the browser prompt, and the web app may be installable.\"\n ],\n \"assumptions\": [\n  \"The responsive web app supports the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.\",\n  \"WCAG 2.1 AA applies to the main flows.\",\n  \"Launch scale is up to 1,000 users and 100,000 records in the first year.\",\n  \"Departure is blocked until every expected route box is scanned and wrong-route boxes are removed or corrected.\",\n  \"Unsent work affected by an offline route change remains available for review and resolution; completed handovers are preserved.\",\n  \"An offline handover completed despite a hold or recall conflict is retained, flagged, and associated with a quality case when synchronized.\",\n  \"Denied or unavailable browser location does not block a handover and is recorded as unavailable.\",\n  \"Live temperature, alert, box-association, and history data are supplied through an existing gateway API or feed.\",\n  \"A signer confirms identity using the sign-in method configured for that account.\",\n  \"Customer portal times use the user's configured account time zone.\",\n  \"Recall responses may leave a remainder unaccounted until later accounting or signed write-off.\",\n  \"Handover signatures and delivery photos are retained for seven years, matching audit-record retention.\",\n  \"A Quality Manager is authorized to sign a write-off.\",\n  \"Refusals are recorded by whole box, with a reason for each refused box.\",\n  \"One configured set of tier limits and allowances applies to all products.\",\n  \"Reports use on-screen date-range filters and CSV export; no custom report builder is included.\",\n  \"Quality-decision escalation and recall notices/reminders are email-only from fixed templates, with no SMS or push.\",\n  \"The customer portal and certificates support English and Arabic, including right-to-left Arabic layout.\",\n  \"The existing logger/gateway data and API/feed are supplied for consumption by the web app.\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"findings\" kind=\"findings\" sha=\"\">\n[\n \"[critic high] REQ-16 The REQ-16 requirement only adds a justification when a decision opposes the recommendation, but AC-16.4 also requires both participants, which contradicts the single-person flow that AC-16.1 allows for first-tier excursions with allowance left.\",\n \"[critic high] REQ-26 AC-26.1 expects the service to return other organisations' orders and the screen to filter them out, which accepts other customers' data (PII) reaching the browser, contrary to the API-side access-scope rule in the out-of-scope list.\",\n \"[critic high] REQ-32 REQ-32 and AC-32.1 refer to 'the specified excursion, refusal/destruction, delivery, decision-time, expiry, and recall measures' and 'every specified report measure', but no measures are defined anywhere, so the criterion cannot be checked.\",\n \"[critic high] REQ-12 Queued work, including signatures and photos (PII), is kept on the device after sign-out, but there is no rule for a different user signing in on the same browser, for whether that user can see or send the work, or for when the cache is cleared.\",\n \"[critic high] REQ-30 Audit trail, lot history, reports, opening inventory, excursion review, quality decisions and delivery evidence (REQ-30/31/32/33/15/16/34) have no access-denied criterion; only account management and recalls define what an unauthorised user sees.\",\n \"[critic high] REQ-27 There is no criterion stopping a customer from opening or downloading certificates (REQ-27/28) or delivery evidence for another organisation's deliveries, for example by changing the delivery ID in the URL.\",\n \"[critic high] REQ-24 Q-3 says an unaccounted remainder stays open 'until it is later accounted for', but no requirement lets a customer change or add to an earlier recall response, so that state change cannot happen.\",\n \"[round trip] not asked for: Show drivers only their assigned routes for today, with stops in route order.\",\n \"[round trip] not asked for: Compare scanned shipper boxes with expected boxes before departure, report missing and wrong-route boxes, and block departure until all expected boxes are scanned and wrong-route boxes are removed or corrected.\",\n \"[round trip] not asked for: Show dispatchers each route stop’s status and last-updated time.\",\n \"[round trip] not asked for: Show each route box’s latest available temperature, status, and alerts from gateway data, and mark cached temperature data as stale while disconnected.\",\n \"[round trip] not asked for: For boxes on hold, display “Do not deliver” and the returned hold reason, and prevent their handover while permitting handover of deliverable boxes.\",\n \"[round trip] not asked for: When online, display “Do not deliver” and prevent handover of any scanned box reported as recalled.\",\n \"[round trip] not asked for: If browser location is denied or unavailable, allow an otherwise eligible handover and record location as unavailable.\",\n \"[round trip] not asked for: While offline, retain loading, handover, and refusal work locally across session expiry or sign-out; after connectivity returns, send queued work automatically, requiring re-authentication if needed, preserving handover occurrence time, and reusing the same handover identifier on retries.\",\n \"[round trip] not asked for: When an assigned route changes while a driver is offline, show route differences, require review and resolution of affected unsent work before continuing, and preserve completed offline handovers.\",\n \"[round trip] not asked for: When an offline handover conflicts with a hold or recall upon synchronization, retain and flag the handover and display the returned quality-case result.\",\n \"[round trip] not asked for: Require identity confirmation using the account’s sign-in method and a reason when a user signs a quality decision; show signed decisions as read-only with a separate superseding-decision action and display both earlier and superseding signed records in history.\",\n \"[round trip] not asked for: When the service returns a quality disposition, show resulting stock, order, and route status and earlier and current dispositions when superseded; show errors and unchanged statuses when a superseding disposition is rejected.\",\n \"[round trip] not asked for: Collect destruction date, quantity, and witness for rejected stock, and prevent entry of a quantity greater than the displayed rejected quantity.\",\n \"[round trip] not asked for: Identify decisions waiting more than four hours as escalated in the Quality Manager’s waiting-decisions view.\",\n \"[round trip] not asked for: Provide eligible Quality Managers a flow to start and close recalls with signed actions; recall start collects product, one or more lots, reason, and severity, and the screen displays each returned result.\",\n \"[round trip] not asked for: Display the returned recall trace, including warehouse locations, boxes, routes, customer deliveries, quantities, delivery dates, receivers, and the trace total alongside received quantity when supplied.\",\n \"[round trip] not asked for: Show customers recall notices in the portal, link them to affected deliveries, and provide a response entry point.\",\n \"[round trip] not asked for: Show customers only their organisation’s current and past orders, allocated lots and expiry dates, order status, and in-transit delivery arrival and temperature status, without exposing other route customers.\",\n \"[round trip] not asked for: Provide a PDF certificate for each completed delivery containing products, lots, expiry dates, quantities, receiver, handover time, each box’s temperature chart from sealing to handover, excursions, and signed excursion decisions.\",\n \"[round trip] not asked for: When late readings produce a new certificate version, list new and earlier versions and keep each available for download.\",\n \"[round trip] not asked for: Present the customer portal and certificates in the user’s selected English or Arabic; render Arabic right to left, including tables and charts, and show dates and times in the account’s configured time zone.\",\n \"[round trip] not asked for: Provide an audit-trail screen showing returned entries with actor, time, changed fields, old and new values, and supplied reason; support filters by record, user, date range, and action type and export of the filtered view.\",\n \"[round trip] not asked for: Show the returned history of a lot from receipt through delivery or destruction in time order.\",\n \"[round trip] not asked for: Provide on-screen reports for selected date ranges and warehouses, with CSV export of displayed figures, including specified excursion, refusal/destruction, delivery, decision-time, expiry, and recall measures; limit warehouse choices to the staff user’s access scope.\",\n \"[round trip] not asked for: Support the latest two browser versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox; make the main flows conform to WCAG 2.1 AA; render the full recall trace returned for the assumed launch scale; and support the assumed first-year product scale and requested lot-trace screen response time.\"\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<untrusted_document id=\"request\" source=\"cli\">\nThe driver sees today's route with its stops in order. Before leaving, the driver scans each shipper box\nonto the vehicle. The application warns about a box that belongs to another route or a box that is\nmissing.\n\nDuring the route the application shows the current temperature and status of each box and any alerts.\n\nAt a stop the driver scans the boxes for that stop. If a box holds stock that is On Hold, the application\nshows \"Do not deliver\" for that box and does not allow it to be handed over. For the remaining boxes,\nthe driver records the receiver's name, captures their signature and a photo of the delivered boxes,\nand completes the handover. The time and location are recorded automatically.\n\nA receiver may refuse all or part of a delivery. The driver records what was refused and a reason, and\nrefused boxes return to the warehouse, where they are Quarantined.\n\nEverything above shall work without a connection. Work done offline is sent when the connection\nreturns. If the route was changed while the driver was offline, the driver is shown the difference before\ncontinuing, and a handover already completed offline is never lost or undone.\n\nAcceptance Criteria\n\n● The driver sees only their own routes.\n● Loading requires every box on the route to be scanned, and a wrong or missing box is reported.\n● A box with stock On Hold cannot be handed over, and the driver sees the reason.\n● A handover records receiver name, signature, photo, time and location.\n● A partial or full refusal can be recorded with a reason per box.\n● Loading, handover and refusal work without a connection and are sent automatically later.\n● A handover recorded offline keeps the time it actually happened, not the time it was sent.\n● If a hold was placed on a box while the driver was offline and the box was handed over, the\nhandover is kept, the conflict is flagged and a quality case is opened.\n● The same handover sent twice is recorded once.\n● The dispatcher sees each stop's status and the time it was last updated.\n\nUS-010: Decide What Happens to Affected Stock\n\nUser Story\n\nAs a Quality Manager, I want every excursion to end in a recorded, signed decision so that no\naffected product reaches a patient without a responsible person approving it.\n\nDescription\n\nEvery excursion requires a decision for each affected handling unit: Release or Reject.\n\nThe system shows the reviewer the full temperature history, the budget used and remaining per tier,\nand a recommendation: Release when every tier still has allowance left, Reject when any tier is used\nup or a not-permitted range was reached.\n\n● If the excursion stayed within the first tier above or below the band and allowance remains, a\nQuality Officer may decide alone.\n● In every other case, a Quality Officer proposes and a Quality Manager approves. The two shall be\ndifferent people.\n● A decision that goes against the system's recommendation always needs both, and a written\njustification.\n\nEach decision is signed electronically: the person confirms their identity again at the moment of\nsigning and gives a reason. A signed decision cannot be edited. It can only be superseded by a new\nsigned decision, and both remain on record.\n\nRejected stock is removed from available stock and listed for destruction. Destruction is recorded\nwith a date, a quantity and a witness.\n\nAcceptance Criteria\n\n● Stock that is On Hold cannot be allocated, packed, loaded or handed over.\n● The reviewer sees the history, the budget per tier and the system's recommendation.\n● A single-person decision is allowed only in the case described above.\n● The person who proposes a decision cannot approve it, even if they hold both roles.\n● Signing requires the person to confirm their identity again and enter a reason.\n● A signed decision cannot be changed or deleted by anyone, including a System Administrator.\n● Releasing stock returns it to where it was: available, or back on its order and route.\n● Rejecting stock removes it from its order, and the order is reallocated under US-005.\n● Decisions waiting longer than 4 hours are escalated to the Quality Manager.\n● Destroyed quantities can never exceed rejected quantities.\n\nUS-011: Recall a Lot\n\nUser Story\n\nAs a Quality Manager, I want to recall a lot and see every unit accounted for so that no recalled\nproduct stays in use.\n\nDescription\n\nA Quality Manager starts a recall for a product and one or more lot numbers, with a reason and a\nseverity.\n\nStarting a recall immediately:\n\n● Sets all stock of those lots that Meridian holds, in any warehouse, to Recalled.\n● Removes it from every order and stops it being handed over, including boxes already on a van.\n● Lists every customer who received any of those lots, with quantities, delivery dates and receivers.\n● Notifies those customers by email and in the customer portal.\n\nThe trace from lot to every location and customer shall be available within one minute of the request.\n\nEach affected customer responds in the portal with, for each delivery, how many packs are still on\nhand, how many were used or dispensed, and how many were destroyed on site. Packs on hand are\ncollected on a return route and Quarantined on arrival.\n\nA recall can be closed only when every pack of the lot is accounted for: held by Meridian, returned,\nreported used, reported destroyed, or written off as unaccounted with a signed justification.\n\nAcceptance Criteria\n\n● Only a Quality Manager can start or close a recall, and both actions are signed.\n● Recalled stock is blocked across all warehouses at once, including stock that is packed or on a\nroute.\n● A driver on a route sees \"Do not deliver\" for a recalled box as soon as the device is online.\n● The trace lists every warehouse location, box, route and customer delivery for the lot, with\nquantities.\n● The quantities in the trace add up exactly to the total quantity received for the lot.\n● Customers are notified and can respond per delivery.\n● A customer's reported quantities cannot exceed what was delivered to them.\n● Customers who have not responded within 24 hours are reminded, and the Quality Manager sees\nwho is outstanding.\n● Recall progress shows the percentage of packs accounted for.\n● A recall cannot be closed while any pack is unaccounted for without a signed write-off.\n\nUS-012: Follow Orders in the Customer Portal\n\nUser Story\n\nAs a Customer User, I want to follow my deliveries and download proof of their condition so that\nI can accept stock with confidence.\n\nDescription\n\nThe customer portal shows the organisation's orders, their status, the lots and expiry dates allocated,\nand for deliveries on the road the planned arrival time and whether the temperature is in range.\n\nAfter delivery, the customer can download a delivery certificate as a PDF for each delivery. The\ncertificate shows the products, lots, expiry dates and quantities, the receiver and time of handover,\nthe temperature chart for each box from sealing to handover, any excursions and the signed decisions\non them.\n\nThe portal and the certificate are available in English and Arabic according to the user's preference.\n\nAcceptance Criteria\n\n● A customer sees current and past orders of their own organisation only.\n● A delivery on the road shows its planned arrival time and an in-range or out-of-range status,\nwithout revealing other customers on the route.\n● A delivery certificate can be downloaded for every completed delivery.\n● The certificate contains the contents by lot, the handover details, the temperature chart, and any\nexcursions with their decisions.\n● A certificate issued once does not change. If late readings alter the history, a new version is\nissued and both remain available.\n● All dates and times are shown in the customer's own time zone.\n● Switching to Arabic turns the whole portal right to left, including tables, charts and the certificate.\n\nUS-013: Audit Trail\n\nUser Story\n\nAs an Auditor, I want a complete, unalterable record of who did what and when so that Meridian\ncan demonstrate compliance during an inspection.\n\nDescription\n\nThe system shall record every creation, change and deletion of regulated data: products and profiles,\nstock, orders and allocations, boxes and routes, handovers, excursions, decisions, recalls, users and\nroles, and configuration.\n\nEach entry records who, when, what was changed, the old and new values, and the reason where one\nwas given. Actions taken by the system itself, such as automatic holds and allocations, are recorded\nas such.\n\nAudit entries cannot be edited or deleted by anyone. It shall be possible to demonstrate that the trail\nhas not been altered.\n\nAll times are stored in a single reference time and shown in the viewer's time zone. Karachi and\nLahore share one time zone and Dubai is in another.\n\nRecords shall be kept for 7 years.\n\nAcceptance Criteria\n\n● Every change to regulated data produces an audit entry with who, when, old value, new value and\nreason.\n● Automatic actions are recorded and attributed to the system.\n● No user, including a System Administrator, can edit or delete an audit entry.\n● An alteration made to the audit trail outside the application can be detected.\n● The audit trail can be filtered by record, user, date range and type of action.\n● An Auditor can export any filtered view.\n● The full history of one lot, from receipt to delivery or destruction, can be viewed in one place in\ntime order.\n\nUS-014: Reports and Scheduled Summaries\n\nUser Story\n\nAs a Quality Manager, I want regular reports on excursions, wastage and delivery performance so\nthat I can find and fix weak points in the cold chain.\n\nDescription\n\nA daily summary shall be emailed at 07:00 warehouse time to the Quality Officers of each warehouse,\nlisting excursions in the last 24 hours, decisions still waiting, silent devices and stock On Hold.\n\nA monthly report shall be generated on the first day of each month and emailed to configured\nstakeholders. It should include, at a minimum:\n\n● Number and rate of excursions by route, driver, vehicle and shipper box type.\n● Packs rejected and destroyed, by product and by cause.\n● Deliveries on time and in full, as a percentage.\n● Average time from excursion to decision.\n● Stock within 60 days of expiry, by product and warehouse.\n● Open recalls and their progress.\n\nThe same figures shall be available on screen for any date range, filterable by warehouse.\n\nAcceptance Criteria\n\n● The daily summary is sent at 07:00 in each warehouse's own time zone.\n● The monthly report is generated automatically on the first day of the month and emailed to the\nconfigured stakeholders.\n● Report figures match the underlying records for the same period.\n● A delivery counts as on time when handed over within 60 minutes of its planned arrival, and as in\nfull when every ordered pack was handed over.\n● Reports can be viewed on screen for any date range and exported.\n● A staff member sees report figures only for their own warehouses.\n\nOut of Scope for Phase 1\n\n● Pricing, invoicing and payments. These remain in Meridian's accounting system.\n● Working out the best order of stops on a route.\n● Purchasing from manufacturers and forecasting demand.\n● Automatic penalties for drivers or customers.\n● Transfers of stock between warehouses.\n● The logger hardware and the supplier's gateway, which already exist.\n</untrusted_document>\n\nRepair this spec so every finding is fixed. Keep requirement IDs stable where the meaning doesn't change. Change nothing the findings don't need. Never fix a finding by moving requested behaviour out of scope or deleting the requirements that cover an intent span.\nAnswer with the changes only, not the whole spec: \"requirements\" holds each requirement you change or add, whole, with all of its acceptance criteria; \"nfrs\" each NFR you change or add; \"removed\" the ids you delete; \"outOfScope\" and \"assumptions\" the whole list, only when it changes. Everything you leave out stays exactly as it is."}